  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the woman with polished nails as the subject of the meme's absurd analogy",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the woman with polished nails, as she is the central figure in the meme's satirical comparison. The user is implicitly identifying with her as the 'victim' or 'subject' of the metaphorical 'crime against the polish' that is equated with starting WW2. This projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but is implied through the user's engagement with the meme's structure, where the woman's actions (removing polish) are the starting point for the absurd analogy. The user sees themselves as part of the 'normal' act (removing polish) that is then grotesquely escalated by the meme's text.",
